    "topByScore": 3,
    "rationale": "3-state GaussianHMM (NORMAL / STRESS BUILDING / CRISIS) is the production architecture when the decoded path is persistent. 2-state (NORMAL / CRISIS) is more stable but cannot express a building-stress early-warning state. 4-state (RISK ON / TRANSITION / STRESS / CRISIS) is rejected when it stays in a warning state most days (crash-hunting) even if recall looks high. States are mapped by observable stress (PC1, HY OAS, vol, drawdown), never by HMM index. Transition matrix is sticky (self-transition 0.97, not re-estimated) so regimes persist."
  },
